{"path":"experimental/ranges/concepts/DerivedFrom","title":"std::experimental::ranges::DerivedFrom","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::ranges::</span>DerivedFrom","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/concepts/DerivedFrom","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"The concept DerivedFrom<T, U> is satisfied if and only if U is a class type that is either T or a public and unambiguous base of T.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/ranges/concepts\">&lt;experimental/ranges/concepts&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-ranges\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> U <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>concept <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> DerivedFrom <span class=\"sy1\">=</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_base_of\"><span class=\"kw593\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_base_of</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U, T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_convertible\"><span class=\"kw597\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_convertible</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_cv\"><span class=\"kw602\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_cv_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_cv\"><span class=\"kw602\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_cv_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-ranges-ts t-mark-ts\">(ranges TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The concept <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">DerivedFrom<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> is satisfied if and only if <code>U</code> is a class type that is either <code>T</code> or a public and unambiguous base of <code>T</code>.\n</p><p>Despite the use of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_base_of\">std::is_base_of</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_convertible\">std::is_convertible</a></span> in its description above, <code>DerivedFrom</code> is not required to use it in its implementation. Thus, there need not be any subsumption relationship between <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">DerivedFrom<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_base_of\"><span class=\"kw593\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_base_of</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U,T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span></span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_convertible\"><span class=\"kw597\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_convertible</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_cv\"><span class=\"kw602\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_cv_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_cv\"><span class=\"kw602\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_cv_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_base_of\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_base_of</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   checks if a type is a base of the other type  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_convertible\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_convertible</span><span>is_nothrow_convertible</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   checks if a type can be converted to the other type  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/ranges","title":"Extensions for ranges"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::ranges::DerivedFrom","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. The concept DerivedFrom<T, U> is satisfied if and only if U is a class type that is either T or a public and…"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"is_base_of","note":"checks if a type is a base of the other type"},{"label":"is_convertible, is_nothrow_convertible","note":"checks if a type can be converted to the other type"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount":114,"codeBlockCount":0}
